   "t_ms": 10,
   "markdown": "# Line cut: Gombe to Damaturu to Maiduguri 330 kV line\n\nSignal: TCN noticed the cut at 01:44 on 21 September 2024 (Nairametrics, 23 Sep 2024, quoting TCN). It names Maiduguri and Damaturu; the city build maps 745.1 km of 330 kV line and 2,707 towers on the corridor.\n\n## Run order for Maiduguri, before the outage length is known (60 days, the brief's two months)\n- 109 sites funded by the Maiduguri plan run on their own solar + storage: 70.1% of critical service-hours kept against 6.9% with nothing built.\n- 170 sites go dark unless fuelled. Fuel these first, most hours per litre:\n  1. Falala Maternity Hospital (health): 2929 critical service-hours for 172.9 litres\n  2. Garba Buzu Idp Camp Health Clinic (health): 2930 critical service-hours for 172.9 litres\n  3. Atal Medical Centre (health): 2929 critical service-hours for 172.9 litres\n  4. Alpine Speciaistl Hospital (health): 2929 critical service-hours for 172.9 litres\n  5. New Gra Primary Health Centre (health): 2934 critical service-hours for 173.4 litres\n- The first 10 on that list need 1732 litres; every dark site needs 69,896 litres, about N229,081,060 at N3,277.47 per litre.\n- Damaturu, also on the line, has no plan built: 0% of its critical service-hours are kept with no backup.\n\n## Closed\n\nRestored at 14:01 on 31 October 2024 (Arise News, 2 Nov 2024, quoting TCN's GM Public Affairs Ndidi Mbah): 40.51 days out, closed on the 40 day window. Over it the plan keeps 70.4% of Maiduguri's critical service-hours against 7% with nothing built, and its systems avoid 12,464 litres of diesel.\n\nSignals are TCN statements quoted by the press. The plan is a scenario; supply and loads are modelled, not measured.",
